LAST_SUCCESS=Task 114 P2.3b DONE: vendored REAL OpenCoreGraphics + merged CGContext, device-verified (Pixel 2 XL). repros/swift-canvas-spike/Sources/OpenCoreGraphics/ = actual upstream OCG library target (MIT, VENDORED.txt) with its empty CGContext.swift replaced by the wasi:canvas body + added CGColor (OCG lacks one). Guest draws via OCG's own CGPath/PathElement/CGLineCap + Foundation CGPoint/CGRect (OCG gets base CG types from @_exported import Foundation). Same scene renders on device via genuine OpenCoreGraphics. BUILD: OCG pulls Foundation/CoreFoundation -> wasm needs WASI emulation (build.sh: -Xcc -D_WASI_EMULATED_{SIGNAL,MMAN,PROCESS_CLOCKS} + -Xlinker -lwasi-emulated-{signal,mman,process-clocks}); COST = component ~7MB->~60MB (Foundation heavy on wasm). Self-contained no-Foundation CoreGraphicsWasi variant (7MB) is in git history (commit c841c4cf).
NOTES=P2.3 remaining: gradients (graphics.linear/radial-gradient), images (decode-image/draw-image-rect), clipping (clip-rect/clip-path), text (glyphs/layout); 3 mapping gaps (dash/offset-shadow/mask-clip). Production size concern: real OCG drags full Foundation (60MB) — for a real guest, slim no-Foundation geometry shim OR strip. Deploy loop: ./build.sh -> stage /tmp/swiftcanvas.wandrpkg -> adb push -> wandr-host --install -> wandr-arbiter kill+launch wandr.swift.canvas.test -> adb exec-out screencap. WSLg desktop: WINIT_UNIX_BACKEND=x11. SwiftUI (OpenRenderBox+OpenSwiftUI+text) out of scope.
